    "label": "82",
    "prompt": "Solve the inequality $\\left|3-|x-2|\\right|\\le 1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-2\\le x\\le 0$ or $4\\le x\\le 6$.\n\nApply the outer absolute value inequality to obtain $2\\le |x-2|\\le 4$, then solve the two signed intervals.",
      "worked": "Apply the algebraic rule to the outer absolute value.\n$$\\begin{align*}-1 &\\le 3-|x-2|\\le 1\\\\2 &\\le |x-2|\\le 4\\end{align*}$$\nSplit into the two signed intervals.\n$$\\begin{align*}-4 &\\le x-2\\le -2 \\quad\\text{or}\\quad 2\\le x-2\\le 4\\\\-2 &\\le x\\le 0 \\quad\\text{or}\\quad 4\\le x\\le 6\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
